          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence"} spectral sequence
            is called
            %em multiplicative
            or a
            %em spectral ring
            if there is a bi-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+algebra"} graded algebra
            structure on each page such that the differentials act as graded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivations"} derivations
            of total degree 1.
          %p
            For example the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+spectral+sequence"} Serre
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah-Hirzebruch+spectral+sequence"} Atiyah-Hirzebruch spectral sequence
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ring spectrum
          %h2#constructions Constructions
          %h3#from_spectral_products_on_cartaneilenberg_systems From spectral products on Cartan-Eilenberg systems
